{"step_index":12377,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T18:06:52Z","thinking":"Considering how to independently verify CPU utilization data reported by the system, excluding any reliance on the server itself or custom scripts, the goal is to identify three separate methods. One approach could involve examining system-level tools for CPU monitoring. Another could involve using external performance analysis utilities running on a separate host. Finally, the third verification could potentially involve observing the behavior of processes using standard Linux utilities to confirm reported utilization.\n\n\nAnalyzing three distinct methods for CPU utilization verification reveals an initial approach using direct kernel data, specifically by calculating jiffies deltas from the system's `/proc/stat`. The second method employs industry-standard system utilities designed for multi-core analysis, deriving utilization from the reported idle percentages. Finally, the third will involve aggregating per-process CPU consumption, comparing this bottom-up view to the top-down perspective from the first two approaches.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport time\\n\\ndef read_proc_stat():\\n    cores = {}\\n    with open('/proc/stat', 'r') as f:\\n        for line in f:\\n            if line.startswith('cpu'):\\n                parts = line.split()\\n                name = parts[0]\\n                # user, nice, system, idle, iowait, irq, softirq, steal\\n                vals = [float(x) for x in parts[1:8]]\\n                idle = vals[3] + vals[4]\\n                total = sum(vals)\\n                cores[name] = (total, idle)\\n    return cores\\n\\nt0 = read_proc_stat()\\ntime.sleep(1.0)\\nt1 = read_proc_stat()\\n\\nprint('=== 1. KERNEL /proc/stat RAW CALCULATION ===')\\ntotal_sum_pct = 0.0\\nfor c in ['cpu0', 'cpu1', 'cpu2', 'cpu3']:\\n    tot_delta = t1[c][0] - t0[c][0]\\n    idle_delta = t1[c][1] - t0[c][1]\\n    busy_pct = ((tot_delta - idle_delta) / tot_delta) * 100.0 if tot_delta > 0 else 0.0\\n    total_sum_pct += busy_pct\\n    print(f'  {c}: {busy_pct:.1f}% busy (idle: {(idle_delta/tot_delta)*100.0:.1f}%)')\\n\\noverall_delta = t1['cpu'][0] - t0['cpu'][0]\\noverall_idle = t1['cpu'][1] - t0['cpu'][1]\\noverall_pct = ((overall_delta - overall_idle) / overall_delta) * 100.0\\nprint(f'  Overall System: {overall_pct:.1f}% (Normalized 100% Scale)')\\nprint(f'  Total 4-vCPU Sum: {total_sum_pct:.1f}% / 400.0%')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/azureuser/IrakIroan/azure_file_explorer\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Verifying Way 1 via /proc/stat kernel calculation\"","toolSummary":"\"Way 1: Calculate raw /proc/stat jiffies\""}}]}
